# Red Cabbage Slaw

Based on [https://www.budgetbytes.com/easy-cabbage-slaw](https://www.budgetbytes.com/easy-cabbage-slaw) (wayback unavailable)

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 1/2 head [Red Cabbage]{ ing="red-cabbage" }, thinly sliced (about 4-5 cups)
- [ ] 1 large [Carrot]{ ing="carrot" }, grated
- [ ] 2 [Green Onions]{ ing="green-onions" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] 3 Tbsp [Apple Cider Vinegar]{ ing="apple-cider-vinegar" }
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [Olive Oil]{ ing="olive-oil" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [Honey or Maple Syrup]{ ing="honey-or-maple-syrup" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [Salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [Black Pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }
- [ ] (Optional) 1/4 cup [Cilantro or Parsley]{ ing="cilantro-or-parsley" }, chopped
- [ ] (Optional) 2 Tbsp [Sunflower Seeds]{ ing="sunflower-seeds" } or Sliced Almonds

## Recipe

1. Thinly slice the [red cabbage]{ ing="red-cabbage" }, grate the [carrot]{ ing="carrot" }, and slice the [green onions]{ ing="green-onions" }. Place in a large bowl
1. In a small bowl, whisk together the [apple cider vinegar]{ ing="apple-cider-vinegar" }, [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" }, honey, [salt]{ ing="salt" }, and [pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }
1. Pour the dressing over the [cabbage]{ ing="red-cabbage" } mixture and toss well to coat
1. Let sit for at least 10 minutes to allow the [cabbage]{ ing="red-cabbage" } to soften slightly and the flavors to meld
1. Add optional cilantro and [seeds]{ ing="sunflower-seeds" } just before serving
1. Serve immediately or refrigerate for up to 3 days (flavors improve over time)

## Notes

- The acid in the vinegar will turn the cabbage a bright pink/magenta color
- Great as a topping for tacos, sandwiches, or grain bowls
- For a creamier version, add 2-3 Tbsp of Greek yogurt or mayonnaise
- Can substitute white vinegar or rice vinegar for apple cider vinegar
